                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 7 at 11:03PM HST until September 8 at 1:30AM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "At 1103 PM HST, Doppler radar indicated diminished rainfall over\nKauai. Rain rates are currently less than 1 inch per hour. Most\nrivers and streams have either leveled off or have begun to fall,\nthough flooding impacts continue across the island. The Waimea River,\nhowever, continues to rise in response to significant runoff. Flash\nflooding is therefore increasingly likely along the lower elevations\nof southwest Kauai, including Kekaha, Waimea, Pakala Village and\nvicinity.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by heavy rain.\n\nSOURCE...Gauges reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nThe island of Kauai.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
                "response": "Avoid",
